<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" library="true" id="31bf-eb23-33a-3d65" name="Daemon Library" gameSystemId="28d4-bd2e-4858-ece6" gameSystemRevision="77" revision="9" battleScribeVersion="2.03" type="catalogue" authorName="a">
  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="002f-0e40-9d49-2a22" name="The Ætheric Dominion (X)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="cac0-a762-8967-dd7d" type="min"/>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="243c-846d-6096-63f8" type="max"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule id="bbb3-5b4d-79fb-d4f5" name="The Ætheric Dominion (X)" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" hidden="false">
          <description>An Ætheric Dominion represents one of the innumerable hosts of daemonkind, each of which is sworn to a greater entity that resides within the Warp. Those encompassed by the same dominion share similar features and behaviours, embodying a primordial force or idea given physical form. Most will share identifying features that link them with the inscrutable patron they serve, providing the smallest sense of unity across a daemonic host.
Any unit with the Ætheric Dominion (X) special rule will have a number of additional special rules and abilities specific to their Ætheric Dominion. A unit which includes models with this special rule may only have one variation of the Ætheric Dominion special rule, e.g., Ætheric Dominion (Encroaching Ruin), and no model with this special rule may join a unit which includes any models with a different variation of the Ætheric Dominion (X) special rule.
A unit which includes models with this special rule without a specific Ætheric Dominion listed in brackets must select one Ætheric Dominion from the list that follows during the army selection process (before the start of a battle) for no additional cost and is thereafter treated as having that variation of this special rule. All units within a Detachment must have the same Ætheric Dominion (X) special rule. A Lords of War choice taken from the Ruinstorm Daemon Army List may select any Ætheric Dominion (X) special rule, even if it is different from the one selected by the Primary Detachment.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="ca6c-e8cf-7bc1-eaa0" name="Encroaching Ruin" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" page="3">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="0" field="1b96-95de-21aa-94f4">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="8ed0-3582-f536-c48e" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="3d70-1d54-a791-ac60" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="e4fb-66cd-e07d-609b" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="9508-8124-d34a-500a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="b7db-bf16-47c5-dc05" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="1214-3abe-c6d1-2038" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="945c-b969-75eb-19d9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="1b96-95de-21aa-94f4" type="max"/>
            <constraint type="min" value="0" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="5b94-5ed5-4856-5d3d"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="75f7-f593-1b7b-7746" name="Advanced Reaction: Wave of Decay (Movement Phase)" hidden="false" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">Trigger: Declared in the Movement phase, after an enemy unit ends a move within 12" of a friendly unit aligned to Encroaching Ruin.
Effect: The triggering enemy unit must immediately take a Dangerous Terrain test for every model in the unit (vehicles take a Dangerous Terrain test on a D6 roll of 1 or 2), and any Armour Values on enemy Vehicles within 12" are reduced by -1 until the end of the turn.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule id="4438-874e-901d-f86" name="Encroaching Ruin" hidden="false">
              <description>Detachment Ability: All Melee weapons and ranged weapons used by models in this Detachment gain the Armourbane (Melee) or Sunder special rule (as appropriate to the weapon type), and models gain the Move Through Cover special rule.

Restriction: Models in a Detachment with this Dominion may not deploy via Deep Strike (unless arriving via an explicit scenario or Rite of War rule).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="7c37-eb30-9328-2c36" name="Armourbane (X)" hidden="false" targetId="cb59-f920-f071-7cd4" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Armourbane (Melee)"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
            <infoLink id="1a05-f6a8-7057-e189" name="Sunder" hidden="false" targetId="20e2-75cf-bc16-cd8f" type="rule"/>
            <infoLink id="ed42-d1ea-0e64-ca2e" name="Move Through Cover" hidden="false" targetId="2b6f-bfec-759e-1746" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="c42-1919-c37e-51f0" id="4d2b-fa7e-23d0-80f8" primary="false" name="Encroaching Ruin"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="3d70-1d54-a791-ac60" name="Heedless Slaughter" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" page="3">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="0" field="15a6-3993-5dd2-b14">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ca6c-e8cf-7bc1-eaa0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="8ed0-3582-f536-c48e" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="e4fb-66cd-e07d-609b" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="9508-8124-d34a-500a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="b7db-bf16-47c5-dc05" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="1214-3abe-c6d1-2038" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="945c-b969-75eb-19d9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
            <modifier type="set" field="15a6-3993-5dd2-b14" value="0">
              <comment>Heedless Slaughter: no Psykers in the Detachment</comment>
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="6e0c-29ba-a445-8321" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="15a6-3993-5dd2-b14" type="max"/>
            <constraint type="min" value="0" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="5d04-bd7d-dced-173a"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="da1e-a128-4799-ffeb" name="Advanced Reaction: Blood-Crazed Retaliation (Assault Phase)" hidden="false" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">Trigger: Declared in the Assault phase, immediately after an enemy unit declares a Charge against a friendly unit aligned to Heedless Slaughter.
Effect: Every model in the reacting unit gains the Counter-Attack (1) special rule until the end of the current Assault phase, and adds +1 to its Weapon Skill Characteristic during the ensuing Fight sub-phase.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule id="a57e-1003-3f17-d12e" name="Heedless Slaughter" hidden="false">
              <description>Detachment Ability: Models gain the Rage (2) and Furious Charge (1) special rules.

Restriction: Units in a Detachment with this Dominion may not include any models with the Psyker Unit Sub-type (and may not manifest Psychic Powers or Psychic Weapons).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="42bf-31bf-fcc0-1a66" name="Rage (X)" hidden="false" targetId="564d-3550-ae44-2f99" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Rage (2)"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
            <infoLink id="5ef2-7fa0-8380-4cbf" name="Furious Charge (X)" hidden="false" targetId="2821-9269-862f-0554" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Furious Charge (1)"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
          </infoLinks>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="f074-f60a-9aa6-c52a" id="a3b9-1c8f-9b90-618a" primary="false" name="Heedless Slaughter"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="8ed0-3582-f536-c48e" name="Formless Distortion" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" page="4" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="0" field="3b89-dc3-165b-e9ce">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ca6c-e8cf-7bc1-eaa0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="3d70-1d54-a791-ac60" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
